Mutual funds pool investment; ETFs trade as exchange-listed fund claims with structural and execution differences.|An ETF's market price can temporarily differ from NAV.|ETF price always equals NAV exactly?|No|Yes|Only during trading
Open-end funds issue or redeem under their rules; closed-end funds generally have a fixed capital base and traded shares.|Closed-end units trade below estimated NAV.|The discount necessarily disappears immediately?|No|Yes|Only for bonds
Index funds follow defined exposures; active funds select deviations under mandates.|A low-cost index fund still inherits its benchmark's concentration.|Indexing removes exposure risk?|No|Yes|Only for broad markets
NAV values fund assets less liabilities per unit; fees and implementation affect tracking differences.|Assets ₹110 − liabilities ₹10 over 10 units gives NAV ₹10.|NAV is…?|₹10|₹11|₹12
Fund due diligence examines mandate, team, process, risk, fees, custody, and liquidity.|A top recent performer uses concentrated leverage.|Recent ranking alone is sufficient selection evidence?|No|Yes|Only over three years
Managed accounts and alternative funds vary in ownership structure, access, regulation, fees, and strategies.|A bespoke account holds investor-owned positions; a fund pools interests.|Product labels ensure identical investor rights?|No|Yes|Only domestically
Hedge funds use varied strategies, potentially including leverage, shorting, and derivatives.|A market-neutral strategy can retain financing and model risk.|Hedge funds always hedge every material risk?|No|Yes|Only if diversified
Private equity invests in private ownership, often combining operating changes and leverage with illiquidity.|A buyout's equity return depends on operating cash, debt repayment, and exit price.|Exit multiple expansion is guaranteed?|No|Yes|Only with leverage
VC funds early high-uncertainty companies; growth equity funds later expansion with differing risk profiles.|Several startup failures can coexist with one large winner.|Each investment's payoff is usually predictable?|No|Yes|Only after funding
Private credit lends outside typical public bond markets under negotiated terms.|An illiquid loan pays a higher coupon but has borrower and recovery risk.|Higher coupon means lower risk?|No|Yes|Only with collateral
Distressed strategies analyse troubled claims, legal priority, recovery, and restructuring outcomes.|Buy a ₹100 claim for ₹30 anticipating uncertain recovery.|A low price alone proves a bargain?|No|Yes|Only below face value
REITs and InvITs hold property or infrastructure interests under applicable structures and distribution rules.|Rental or concession cash supports distributions but also maintenance and debt.|Distribution yield equals guaranteed total return?|No|Yes|Only for property
Commodity returns reflect spot exposure, futures mechanics, storage or roll effects, and currency.|A commodity ETF using futures can differ from spot-price performance.|Gold generates contractual interest by itself?|No|Yes|Only when held long term
Infrastructure funds invest in long-lived assets with demand, regulation, construction, and financing risks.|A toll-road investment depends on traffic and concession terms.|Long asset life removes cash-flow uncertainty?|No|Yes|Only for public assets
Collectibles lack standard cash flows and can face appraisal uncertainty, storage costs, and thin trading.|An artwork's auction estimate exceeds the net amount after fees.|Estimated price equals readily available cash?|No|Yes|Only for famous artists
Fund fees and carried interest depend on contractual waterfalls, hurdles, and timing.|20% carry on ₹50 eligible profit gives ₹10 before other terms.|Carry always applies identically to all cash distributions?|No|Yes|Only in private equity
Commitments are promised capital; calls draw it; early costs can produce a J-shaped return path.|Commit ₹100 but only ₹30 is called initially.|The investor should plan liquidity for…?|Uncalled commitments as well|Only called amounts|Only current NAV
MOIC compares total value with invested capital; DPI realised distributions; RVPI remaining value; TVPI combines them; IRR incorporates timing.|Paid-in ₹100, distributions ₹40, residual ₹90 gives TVPI 1.3×.|TVPI here is…?|1.3×|0.4×|0.9×
Private assets face illiquidity, subjective interim values, and selection bias.|A dataset excludes failed funds and uses smoothed appraisals.|Reported risk and returns may be…?|Biased|Guaranteed accurate|Independent of sample selection
